diff --git a/PORTING.md b/PORTING.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d20d456aecea901cc41b1f11fa667161c523a044
--- /dev/null
+++ b/PORTING.md
@@ -0,0 +1,354 @@
+# MCHorizonWiiU
+
+Porting Horizon 26.3 to the Nintendo Wii U. The project repository is [MCHorizonWiiU](https://github.com/megabytesme/MCHorizonWiiU); Horizon source is kept at the repository root, and Wii U entry-point, platform, and renderer work lives under `wiiu/`.
+
+## Status
+
+- Horizon upstream is checked out at `69fab597a6f0e8a6ce524d38d1b73e599e343034` (`main`, 2026-11-06).
+- The read-only reference `$workspace\Codex\MCHorizonUWP` has a real native D3D11 FL9_1 rendering path on its `uwp-phone-d3d11` branch (local commit `43c80ed9b`). It accepts Horizon CPU `Frame`/`SectionMesh` data and implements terrain, entities, translucent passes, hand, HUD, depth, atlases and indexed meshes without routing rendering through `wgpu`. The public remote [`history/uwp-native-mipmaps`](https://github.com/megabytesme/MCHorizonUWP/tree/history/uwp-native-mipmaps) branch (`8a7f0148`) contains the same native-renderer architecture; `uwp-phone-d3d11` itself is local-only. The remote backend notes report x64 UWP readback checks and ARM32 compile/strict-link checks, not a verified phone run. This is the renderer reference to adapt architecturally, not a directly reusable graphics backend.
+- Horizon's `horizon-client-render` crate owns the standard concrete `wgpu` renderer. The UWP reference added a `PresentationBackend` / `TerrainBackend` seam and a separate D3D11 renderer that consumes CPU `Frame`/`SectionMesh` data. Reuse that seam design for GX2; implement GX2-specific shaders, buffers, texture atlases, depth state and draw submission rather than calling `wgpu` or copying D3D11 code.
+- The old `rust-wiiu/wut` Rust crate was archived on 2026-02-20. The current rust-wiiu organization is experimental, Linux-only, and has moved to `cafe-sys`, `cafe-target-spec`, a Rust fork, and `cargo-wiiu`. Book for U warns that its guide is being rewritten.
+- WSL Ubuntu has upstream Rust nightly, `cargo-wiiu` 0.4.1, and the official devkitPro WUT `wiiu-dev` package. The project builds a Rust `no_std` static library, initializes WUT/GX2 for TV and GamePad, and packages RPX/WUHB. Horizon's `horizon-core` `wiiu-core` feature now exposes `BlockPos`/`SectionPos`/`ChunkPos`, its Java-compatible random streams, and its production Perlin noise sampler without `std`; `alloc`-based noise APIs link through a WUT/newlib `malloc`/`free` allocator. A new `horizon-terrain-data` crate shares the exact 24-byte `TerrainVertex` format between desktop and Wii U code. The default `build.sh` path now uses the Cafe-`std` worldgen bridge: it loads Horizon's registry, terrain assets, biome data, and `horizon-world` generator, then meshes runtime proto-chunks with Horizon's original `horizon-terrain-mesh::Mesher` before GX2 submission. The default-path Cafe cross-build and RPX/WUHB packaging pass. The latest VPAD diagnostic package loaded in Cemu and logged `Run title` (checksum `0x96bb4616`); no frame or input was verified. The explicitly selected no-worldgen fixture is separate diagnostic code, not the client path. Capture builds consume real captured `SectionMesh::solid` data and the captured sprite atlas/lightmap. The GX2 adapter expands quads to triangle lists and converts fixed-point UVs, light coordinates, and packed RGBA to GX2 floats. Depth testing is enabled for TV and GamePad contexts; translucent meshes remain unsupported.
+- The adapter consumes actual `SectionMesh::solid` vertices from Horizon's render capture. `tools/horizon_wiiu_capture.py` ranks nonempty sections by camera distance, decodes their host-endian 24-byte records, combines the nearest sections within a vertex budget, rebases them around one camera-relative origin, and emits target-compiled C constants. Captures include Horizon's current block sprite atlas, 16×16 RGBA lightmap, and view parameters. The latest scratch Horizon 26.3 creative capture contains 5,412 sections, 98,236,704 mesh bytes, 21,315,584 sprite bytes, and 1,024 lightmap bytes. The converter selects 17 sections at the default 65,536-vertex budget, using 24 sprite layers packed into a guarded 330×330 RGBA atlas. The GX2 fragment shader bilinearly samples the captured colored lightmap per fragment using interpolated vertex sky/block coordinates; lighting is fixed to the captured frame. Capture builds use the captured yaw, pitch, FOV, and aspect ratio with Horizon's zero-to-one depth projection. The left stick and D-pad move relative to the view; the right stick changes yaw and pitch. Cemu 2.6 loaded the lightmap RPX and ran the title (checksum `0x55b4b4b8`). This verifies conversion, cross-compilation, packaging, and RPX startup, not a Horizon menu, verified terrain frame, or GamePad controls. Translucent meshes remain unsupported.
+
+## Build and emulator results
+
+### Cafe gameplay atomics (2026-11-08)
+
+- `crates/horizon-client/Cargo.toml`, `src/lib.rs`, and the four gameplay source locations using private 64-bit atomics select the existing portable-atomic fallback without native 64-bit atomics; the related test-fixture counter uses the same alias. Desktop retains standard atomics and all signed arithmetic and memory ordering are unchanged. These are localized upstream substitutions at the actual definitions. A disposable renderer-gated Cafe check eliminated the four corresponding gameplay atomic errors, but still had 45 window/renderer interface errors and did not compile the test fixture. On WSL with `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$scratch/horizonwiiu-cit-work`, `cargo test --offline -p horizon-client --lib --no-default-features native_lifecycle::tests --jobs 32` passed 7/7, and the same test binary passed the exact entity-model, occlusion-worker and dispenser tests. No full Cafe client or hardware runtime result is implied.
+
+### Cafe client-library atomics (2026-11-07)
+
+- `crates/horizon-client-lib/Cargo.toml`, `crates/horizon-client/src/client_lib.rs`, and the existing client-library source locations using private 64-bit atomics select the existing portable-atomic fallback when the target lacks native 64-bit atomics. Desktop retains the original standard atomics; signed sentinels and memory orderings are unchanged. These localized substitutions are required at the upstream definitions and should reapply with their containing modules. A disposable renderer-gated Cafe check no longer reported the 17 prior atomic errors but still stopped at an unrelated Discord error (subsequently addressed separately); this was not a full client build. A separately linked Cemu probe tested signed compare-exchange and four concurrent high-bit-set u64 counters with `failure_flags=0`; source and logs are under `%TEMP%\HorizonWiiU-client-atomic-probe-fde939a343664553bac297e6aeb43330`. On WSL with `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$scratch/horizonwiiu-cit-work`, `cargo test --offline -p horizon-client-lib --lib --no-default-features a_silent_client_times_out --jobs 32` passed 2/2, and the same test binary passed the exact recorder-lifecycle and concurrent-UUID tests. No Wii U hardware or full-client runtime result is implied.
+
+### Cafe Discord presence boundary (2026-11-07)
+
+- `crates/horizon-client/src/discord_presence.rs` skips the optional Discord worker on Cafe and returns `Unsupported` for its unavailable local IPC. This gate belongs at the existing worker and IPC call sites because Cafe has no compatible opener; desktop behavior is unchanged and the localized patch should be straightforward to reapply. A scratch harness ran six original host tests, including Unix-socket interactions, and type-checked the Cafe module and its unavailable-path test. The harness is under `%TEMP%\HorizonWiiU-discord-cafe-probe-5d910353919d4224a589f1fdd8f43ba7`; no Cafe runtime or full-client result is implied.
+
+### Cemu instruction and panorama diagnostics (2026-11-07)
+
+- A diagnostic using Horizon's original panorama face loader stalls in `png::Decoder::read_info`; scratch instrumentation narrowed this to code emitted for depth/transform selection. A separate C-only WUT RPX executing `crnand 20,6,1` reaches its before marker but not its after marker in stock Cemu 2.6 and the NSS-patched build. A `nop` control reaches both markers; the result also reproduces with an isolated single-core-interpreter profile. The user first tried a bare RPX and then a WUHB containing that RPX on Aroma; both showed system-memory error 160-2203 without a diagnostic log. The probe source is under `%TEMP%\HorizonWiiU-crnand-standalone` and the Cemu logs under `%TEMP%\HorizonWiiU-Panorama-Cemu-bc28b7eae7e34cf3b409c50e2bd39b43`; the corrected WUHB remains at `/wiiu/apps/horizon-crnand-diagnostic` on the SD card. See `%TEMP%\HorizonWiiU-crnand-hardware-36ea292c1507457bb1be7af0b86e182a\README.txt` for diagnostic interpretation and limitations.
+- A temporary compiler-code-generation perturbation got the panorama probe past the decoder and into GX2 draws, but sampled pixels did not match expected values. This does not establish a safe fix or a correct panorama. The unverified platform and probe sources are preserved under `%TEMP%\HorizonWiiU-panorama-experiment-9e09175660d1466d888fd8c5552b9459`; the original Horizon source remains unchanged. The separately tested Loading artwork-callback experiment is also uncommitted at `%TEMP%\horizonwiiu-loading-artwork-callback-experiment.patch` until a real Cafe host can use it.
+- COM3 was confirmed as the CH340, configured at the user's 57600 8-N-1/no-flow settings, and opened for receive-only capture through an elevated local SSH session. The Wii U's serial log identifies the first hardware diagnostic failure as loader error `-470005`: the RPX imports the nonexistent `__rplwrap_exit` symbol and never reaches `main`. A scratch repack with devkitPro `elf2rpl` imports `coreinit.exit` instead and preserves the linked executable code. The corrected WUHB's real Wii U SD log contains both `before crnand` and `after crnand`, proving this instruction returned on hardware; the user reported that its loading screen remained afterward, so clean return to the menu is not established. The Cemu instruction stall is therefore not reproduced by this hardware probe. This packaging fix must not be generalized to the Rust bootstrap without checking its import sections.
+- `wiiu/package_rpx.cmake` and the bootstrap, entropy-probe and HUD-probe CMake packaging steps keep `cargo wiiu rpx` for its Rust import-section handling, normalize the linked ELF's `__rplwrap_exit` alias on a copy, and verify `coreinit.exit` and reject remaining wrapper imports before promoting a temporary RPX. Switching the Rust bootstrap directly to `elf2rpl` was rejected: it silently left its import sections as ordinary PROGBITS. The build scripts are Wii U-specific; no Horizon core changes were needed. With the WUT toolchain, WSL `cmake --build $scratch/HorizonWiiU-wrapper-rename-test-20261107/bootstrap-build --parallel` and the analogous `entropy-build` passed; the bootstrap RPX reached its Cafe entry point in isolated Cemu and the mixed Rust entropy-probe diagnostic exited with `failure_flags=0`. Negative missing-exit and unsupported-wrapper tests failed while preserving the previous RPX. These are not full-client or physical-hardware validations of the new packaging path.
+- A separate temp-only GX2 2D-atlas experiment using generated asymmetric cube faces and Horizon's unchanged projection and verified WGSL cube geometry passed 54/54 interior pixel checks in stock Cemu (RGB tolerance 2). It bypasses PNG and the title lifecycle; atlas seam filtering, texture-height limits and hardware behavior remain unverified. Source, oracle and build commands: `%TEMP%\HorizonWiiU-panorama-rgba-1dfc2d3ea56e444c82257b9bd0bd813b\RESULTS.md`. This is not a client or panorama checkpoint.
