+### Cafe renderer atomics (2026-11-07)
+
+- `crates/horizon-client-render/Cargo.toml`, `src/lib.rs`, and the nine source locations using private 64-bit atomics select the existing portable-atomic fallback when the target lacks native 64-bit atomics. This preserves the original values and memory orderings and retains standard atomics on desktop; the upstream files must select the shared type because the atomics are defined there. A disposable source copy with experimental Winit dependency gates exposed twelve atomic errors; after this change those errors disappeared, but unresolved Winit references still prevented the renderer from completing its Cafe check. On WSL in the repository with `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$scratch/horizonwiiu-cit-work CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0`, `cargo +nightly test -p horizon-client-render --lib chunk_map::tests --no-default-features --jobs 16 --offline` passed 7/7. No Cafe runtime or multicore atomic verification is implied. These localized substitutions should be straightforward to reapply, though the nine upstream source locations must be tracked.
