+```sh
+cargo +nightly test -p horizon-terrain-mesh --lib cit_armor::tests --no-default-features --jobs 1
+cargo +nightly test -p horizon-client-render --lib hud::tests::an_armor_rules_texture_is_packed_too --no-default-features --jobs 1
+RUSTC=$workspace/HorizonWiiU-toolchain/rust-wiiu-cafe/build/host/stage1/bin/rustc cargo +nightly check -p horizon-terrain-mesh --no-default-features --target powerpc-nintendo-cafe --jobs 1
+```
+
+The tests passed 8/8 and 1/1, respectively, and the Cafe check passed. The original `cit_armor.rs` moved byte-for-byte and the old renderer paths are re-exported. The pre-existing `.vscode/` folder is untracked and is not part of this work. E: holds the current build cache; do not delete unexpectedly modified temporary trees or other user data without determining ownership.
+
+1. Reach Horizon's existing main menu first. Make the ordinary client entry (`run_with` → `run_loading` → `Loading`/`Title`) run on Cafe; keep the current WUT worldgen bootstrap diagnostic separate and do not make a substitute menu. Treat serial/file logging as a debugging aid for this path, not a milestone ahead of the menu.
+2. Separate the concrete `Renderer` construction and GPU resources from shared frame/menu data, including CPU types still housed in WGPU-bearing modules; make WGPU/Winit optional for the Cafe client while preserving Horizon's current module paths. Connect the tested `wiiu/entropy` startup anchor to the eventual Cafe client and preserve its documented stock-Cemu and real-hardware limitations.
+3. Add the Cafe host/presenter path so CafeOS events drive the existing `Loading`/`StartupMenu` input and GX2 draws the existing `HudBatch`, panorama and title frame. The original `HudAtlas` and `HudBatch` are now shared; connect them to the GX2 presenter and expose the original startup screens to a Cafe host. Feed the VPAD adapter into Horizon's existing `Pads` processing and extract its menu navigation for startup if needed; avoid a second navigation implementation. `Game`/`Loading` still own concrete Winit/WGPU types, so the presentation contracts alone are not selectable on Wii U.
+4. Build and launch that full-client RPX in Cemu; verify a visible Horizon menu frame and menu input with a screenshot/log. RPX `Run title` alone and the current white loading screen do not count as menu success.
+5. After the original menu works, connect Horizon's existing world, player, integrated server, and save paths to the GX2 backend. Cafe std currently implements `File::try_lock` and `unlock` as unsupported (`library/std/src/sys/fs/cafe.rs:409-426`), so Horizon's unchanged `save::SessionLock::acquire` cannot open or create worlds and reports the lock failure. WUT's file-open API does not expose an equivalent lock flag, and Cafe std documents `create_new` as non-atomic; neither a silent bypass nor a lockfile is an equivalent fix. Implement and verify a compatible Cafe locking mechanism before claiming world entry. Keep worldgen diagnostic-only, use Cafe audio behind the existing `sound_engine` boundary, and defer networking until single-player works.
+
+An isolated WUT/Cemu probe confirmed that two distinct Cafe FS clients can hold simultaneous `FSOpenFile("r+")` handles to the same scratch SD file (both returned `FS_STATUS_OK`). The RPX SHA-256 was `597d494a8ee0f15c3bf535087d11d9844af31d82b6dc22e0c6ea123d141a2dbb`; source, build, and result are under `$scratch\horizon-fs-lock-probe`. WUT's `procui.h` also states that a background app retains filesystem access, so foreground switching alone is not a proof of exclusive access. This probe is Cemu-only evidence: it does not establish Wii U hardware semantics or provide a session lock.
+
+References: [Cafe std filesystem implementation](https://github.com/rust-wiiu/rust/blob/62606b70e351edb297db1fdd4b99c8b8ca440d38/library/std/src/sys/fs/cafe.rs#L347-L425), [WUT filesystem flags](https://github.com/devkitPro/wut/blob/master/include/coreinit/filesystem.h), [WUT ProcUI background access](https://github.com/devkitPro/wut/blob/master/include/proc_ui/procui.h), and [Cemu v2.6 FS open dispatch](https://github.com/cemu-project/Cemu/blob/a6fb0a48eb437a8a41c13b782ac8ae0433bf8f98/src/Cafe/IOSU/fsa/iosu_fsa.cpp#L238).
